# User Registration: Spammers

## Tags

* type: bug
* status: open
* priority: high
* assigned: fredm
* interested: alexm, zachs, pjotrp
* keywords: genenetwork, user, registration, user registration

## Description

Some user accounts are spam accounts. We need to deal with them.

Some possible solutions:

* Mandatory account verification (double opt-in): We already do a version of this: we should probably actually make the token unique (it is... mostly) and cryptographically secure (it is not, currently).
* Real-time domain & MX record lookup: Check for valid mail exchanger (MX) records to immediately catch fake domains. Should do this check before attempting to send the token mentioned previously.
* Disposable and temporary email detection: this is also a check we can do before attempting to send the token. Search for open datasets regarding these.
